ose'","'the skill adds no counter, tag vocabulary or state of its own'","ABSENCE: no stated attribution handle (how the next run enumerates exactly the prior run's tickets) given the no-state constraint"],"finding":"The scoring protocol requires the next run to read 'the previous run's tickets' and sum 'the merged diffs of exactly those', but the plan also forbids the skill from introducing 'counter, tag vocabulary or persistent state of its own' — leaving the mechanism by which a run's own tickets are identified/grouped unspecified. An executor cannot determine which tickets belong to 'the previous run' without some grouping handle.","group_criteria":["COH","E2","G6","T8"],"group_id":"g1210c9177f10410a","id":"f69f1e04d700f3221","impact":1.0,"is_primary":true,"location":"The change — 'a run is scored by what LANDED' bullet; AC 'It names the measuring actor and when' / 'It introduces no counter, tag vocabulary or persistent state of its own'","norm_id":"nf9d51ab0a76f9a8e","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The operator opens a successor run; the skill must list 'the previous run's tickets' but has no tag/grouping to select them from the shared pipeline, so it guesses or asks a clarifying question."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Specify an external grouping handle the skill reads but does not own — e.g. the operator records the run's ticket ids on approval, or the run is keyed by its discovery SHA already stated in the plan — so 'the previous run's tickets' resolves to a concrete, state-free list.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Name the pre-existing, non-new handle by which the opening step enumerates exactly the prior run's own tickets (e.g. the already-filed dated 'Janitor Cleanup <YYYY-MM-DD>' epic's children), and state that reusing it introduces no new state.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the NEXT run opens by reading the previous run's tickets and summing the merged diffs of exactly those'","Plan constraint: 'the skill adds no counter, tag vocabulary or state of its own'","Existing ticketization.md:10 already groups a run's children under a dated epic 'Janitor Cleanup <YYYY-MM-DD>' — a pre-existing handle the plan could name without adding new state","ABSENCE: the plan never states how 'exactly those' tickets are enumerated, so the attribution step's data-flow is incomplete"],"finding":"The deferred scoring mechanism requires enumerating EXACTLY the previous run's tickets, but the plan neither names the handle by which a run's own ticket set is identified nor reconciles that with its rule that the skill 'adds no counter, tag vocabulary or state of its own'. Without a named, pre-existing grouping handle, 'summing the merged diffs of exactly those' is under-specified: the opening step cannot deterministically recover which tickets belonged to the prior run.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":"g1210c9177f10410a","id":"f9a11e42883782133","impact":1.0,"is_primary":false,"location":"The change — 'a run is scored by what LANDED ... reading the previous run's tickets and summing the merged diffs of exactly those'; and AC 'It names the measuring actor and when: the next run's opening step'","norm_id":"nc417a60d6f2c8d2b","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two tidying runs happen on nearby dates; the opening step cannot tell which filed tickets belong to which run and double-counts or misses deletions","An operator runs the terminal 'same read' with no successor and has no deterministic criterion for selecting the prior run's tickets"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a clause specifying that a tidying run files its tickets under a dated epic (as the current skill does) and that the opening scoring step reads exactly that epic's children — making the attribution handle an existing artifact, not new state.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify, in the tidying-janitor skill text, the key by which a run's own ticket set is identified for scoring (e.g. reuse the existing dated `Janitor Cleanup <YYYY-MM-DD>` epic as the grouping), reconciling it with the 'no tag vocabulary or state of its own' constraint.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the NEXT run opens by reading the previous run's tickets and summing the merged diffs of exactly those'","Plan: 'the skill adds no counter, tag vocabulary or state of its own, because a skill that exists to remove mechanism must not install one'","Existing ticketization already files a dated grouping: ticketization.md:10 'Create an epic titled `Janitor Cleanup <YYYY-MM-DD>`' — a per-run epic the plan could name as the identification key but does not","ABSENCE: no plan text names the epic/dated grouping (or any other key) as how 'the previous run's tickets' / 'exactly those' are enumerated without a skill-owned tag or state"],"finding":"The run-scoring protocol requires the next run to read 'the previous run's tickets' and sum 'the merged diffs of exactly those,' but the plan forbids the skill any 'tag vocabulary or state of its own' and never specifies the key by which a run enumerates its OWN ticket set — leaving an executor unable to deterministically identify 'exactly those' tickets.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":"g1210c9177f10410a","id":"fbdeea7f9fd9dc12c","impact":1.0,"is_primary":false,"location":"Plan: 'The change — modify, not discard', scoring bullets ('a run is scored by what LANDED, attributed to the run…'; 'the skill adds no counter, tag vocabulary or state of its own'); AC 'It names the measuring actor and when' and 'It introduces no counter, tag vocabulary or persistent state of its own.'","norm_id":"n9c1f7346ce9815db","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The successor run must decide which tickets belong to the prior run; with no tag/state and no stated grouping key, it either invents an ad-hoc heuristic (divergent definitions across runs) or cannot complete the opening scoring step","The operator-driven 'same read over the prior run's tickets' fallback hits the identical ambiguity: which ticket set is 'the prior run's'?"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that the run reuses the existing per-run dated epic (the already-filed 'Janitor Cleanup <YYYY-MM-DD>' grouping — not new skill state) as the enumeration key, and define merge-status as derived from the tracker/main merge state of exactly the children of the prior run's epic. Add an AC that the scoring step names this identification key.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.85,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Note in the plan that the per-ticket attribution metric is the realization of the parent's 'success metric measured by what landed, not tickets filed' intent, superseding the parent's literal 'on main a week later' phrasing, so the refinement is visibly aligned to the parent contract.","cohort":["G7"],"criteria":["G7"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.652,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent operator ruling 2026-11-02, deliverable 6: '...with a per-run ticket budget and a success metric measured on main a week later rather than by tickets filed.'","Leaf: 'A bare main-to-main delta cannot score a tidying run: main moved +54,961/-26,221 over 114 commits ... so a run's few hundred deleted lines are invisible in it.'","Leaf substitutes: 'the NEXT run opens by reading the previous run's tickets and summing the merged diffs of exactly those'","Both honor the parent's 'not by tickets filed' principle; the divergence is only in the measurement locus (per-ticket attribution vs whole-main delta)."],"finding":"The leaf's success-metric mechanism (next run reads the prior run's tickets and sums their merged diffs) refines the parent's literal phrasing 'a success metric measured on main a week later'; the leaf explicitly rejects the main-to-main delta. The parent's load-bearing intent (score by what LANDED, not by tickets filed) is preserved, so this is a wording-level refinement rather than a contradiction, but the leaf should name the realignment so the mismatch against the parent's 'on main a week later' phrasing is not read as silent divergence.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1166909bb3e197f2","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'The change — modify, not discard' (attribution bullet) vs parent epic 77e3 operator ruling deliverable 6","norm_id":"n0b4ca618dc3ccf42","priority":0.198,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reader comparing the leaf's acceptance criterion ('success metric is what merged from the run's own tickets') against the parent's 'measured on main a week later' phrasing could read it as the leaf stepping outside the parent contract."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate examples/agent-skills/README.md as a consumer: add a rebar-tidy skills-table row and update the rebar-janitor/defect-audit row so the index reflects the split.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.315,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["README.md:17 '| `rebar-janitor` |